---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About — Chirag Gandhi" active="about">
  <style>
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.6rem); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    .block { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .block h2 { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .block p { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--body); max-width: 62ch; }
    .block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .block strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
    .block .rule {
      border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }
  </style>

  <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
  <h1>Product manager by day, builder by default.</h1>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Work</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a product manager. My day job is building enterprise products with
      engineering teams — strategy, discovery, delivery, end to end. The formal
      record — companies, numbers, dates — lives on the <a href="/chirag-portfolio/resume">resume</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Personal</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Working on:</strong> the Luxembourg property crawler, this
      portfolio site, a market study run by four agents in one day.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Built:</strong> multi-agent pipelines, crawlers, dashboards, small
      tools — with Claude, Cursor, and OpenClaw.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Learning:</strong> Luxembourgish — which has spawned a few
      projects of its own.
    </p>
    <p>Currently based in Luxembourg.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>The meta</h2>
    <p class="rule">
      A project counts when a stranger can open it. Everything on this site is
      real — each project published as it reaches a shareable state. No
      vaporware, no "coming soon".
    </p>
    <p>My style: build small, ship publicly, iterate. This site is the standing example.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
